# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the value.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is gitignored. This example file is not, so never put a real
# value in here.
#
# The variable is PUBLIC_, meaning Astro inlines it into the static build and
# it is visible in page source. That is correct for a Formspree form ID: the
# endpoint is public by design. Do NOT give any actual secret a PUBLIC_ prefix.
#
# Because it is baked in at build time, changing it needs a rebuild and a
# redeploy. Restarting the dev server is not enough. The same value must also
# be set on the Vercel project under Settings, Environment Variables, because
# Vercel builds remotely and never reads this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Formspree form ID: the part after /f/ in your form's endpoint URL.
# Find it at https://formspree.io, open your form, then Integration. The
# endpoint reads https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxxx and you want just the
# xxxxxxxx part.
#
# Without this the contact form renders disabled with a visible setup notice,
# rather than looking fine and silently dropping every lead.
PUBLIC_FORMSPREE_ID=
